<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If689ffd92f0255847bea2424950da4547b2c0df3" commit="a6ab102cd487a2ba5b6552e5b72ae13809f46623" commit_message="vboot: Remove vboot1 cryptolib padding source  The old vboot1 cryptolib hard-coded many of its padding arrays in a padding.c file.  Use the equivalent vboot2 apis instead.  This change is almost exclusively on the host and test side; the only firmware impact is on a single line of debug output.  BUG=chromium:611535 BRANCH=none TEST=make runtests; emerge-kevin coreboot depthcharge  Change-Id: If689ffd92f0255847bea2424950da4547b2c0df3 Signed-off-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/400902 Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="400902" owner_email="rspangler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/02/400902/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2235f0e84e13fef313afe54e749b73744b157884" commit="3c834fb531e2c6b2ab70c726e40e069a538b4bcd" commit_message="vboot: Remove the remainder of vb1 cryptolib  At this point, all that's left are a few constants in the cryptolib header files, and they're only used by host-side code.  So move them to a host-side header file and get rid of cryptolib.  BUG=chromium:611535 BRANCH=none TEST=make runtests; emerge-kevin coreboot depthcharge  Change-Id: I2235f0e84e13fef313afe54e749b73744b157884 Signed-off-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/400903 Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="400903" owner_email="rspangler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/03/400903/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I75b6014be00c5266545db10e87c1d9485fd1444b" commit="e6ad8db537e0909c89408d05ab657b338956ea87" commit_message="vboot: remove unused stateful_util  Now that the vboot1 cryptolib code is gone, nothing uses stateful_util. Remove it and its unit tests.  BUG=chromium:611535 BRANCH=none TEST=make runtests; emerge-kevin coreboot depthcharge  Change-Id: I75b6014be00c5266545db10e87c1d9485fd1444b Signed-off-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/400904 Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="400904" owner_email="rspangler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/04/400904/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I49ad0e32e38d278dc3589bfaf494bcf0e4b0a4bd" commit="d587dcb4cb975c5e67c5ba461180fdbb41d19d63" commit_message="vboot: use malloc and free directly  Originally, vboot1 code used VbExMalloc() and VbExFree() since it needed to talk to EFI firmware that didn't have standard malloc() and free(). Now, coreboot and depthcharge implement them as wrappers around those standard calls.  vboot2 code already calls them directly, so let vboot1 code do that too.  BUG=chromium:611535 BRANCH=none TEST=make runtests; emerge-kevin coreboot depthcharge  Change-Id: I49ad0e32e38d278dc3589bfaf494bcf0e4b0a4bd Signed-off-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/400905 Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="400905" owner_email="rspangler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/05/400905/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9ee38a819c59cc58a72ead78cf5ddf3d0f301ae7" commit="0d38169fdb85eeaa78428cfb31dbc25867d3ddd3" commit_message="vboot: Add vb2_unpack_key_buffer  Previously, vb2_unpack_key() actually unpacked a key buffer.  Callers that had a vb2_packed_key had to typecast it back to a uint8_t buffer to unpack it.  Rename vb2_unpack_key() to vb2_unpack_key_buffer(), and make vb2_unpack_key() unpack a vb2_packed_key.  BUG=chromium:611535 BRANCH=none TEST=make runtests; emerge-kevin coreboot depthcharge;      emerge-samus and boot it  Change-Id: I9ee38a819c59cc58a72ead78cf5ddf3d0f301ae7 Signed-off-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/400906 Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="400906" owner_email="rspangler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/06/400906/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I901bbeccbfb67ac159edad2ee7e14868dba73165" commit="252a6318e33e4b6dc341284a2c3dff6fa884590d" commit_message="coreboot: move asset loactions for pyro  Start using the assets from the shared basedboard-reef location.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:*301320,CL:*301435 BUG=chrome-os-partner:58868 BRANCH=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I901bbeccbfb67ac159edad2ee7e14868dba73165 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/405631 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="405631" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/31/405631/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I853629a8ba3ac8a16f68e6a9ddd7ba881723d768" commit="41851699852e519e16fb443abd808f0676bef3fb" commit_message="bmpblk: Remove eve board  Remove the eve board until the bmpblk package is updated first.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:58666 TEST=emerge-eve chromeos-bmpblk  Change-Id: I853629a8ba3ac8a16f68e6a9ddd7ba881723d768 Signed-off-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/405833 Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="405833" owner_email="dlaurie@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/33/405833/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia669a1e1f0931bfeeab64e5ab34b414f0745f699" commit="479ed4481dcf2f6701c65c4ea4f59a84bd25244e" commit_message="container_utils: swap device_jail threads  Use the other thread to run the CUSE message loop, and the main thread to run the PermissionBrokerClient. This allows us to avoid all of the stupid threading gymnastics and get rid of dependencies in PBC.  BUG=chromium:644338 TEST=cat an unclaimed device and check for data  Change-Id: Ia669a1e1f0931bfeeab64e5ab34b414f0745f699 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/405369 Commit-Ready: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chirantan Ekbote &lt;chirantan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="405369" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/69/405369/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit bran